---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro:components";

---

<Layout title="Home">
  <h1>Examples of the use of Astro's built-in Image component</h1>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="single-image/">Static Image From import (Local)</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="group-of-images/">Group of images from an import glob (Local)</a>
    </li>
    <li><a href="single-remote-image/">Image from a URL (Remote)</a></li>
    <li><a href="group-of-remote-images/">Images from URLs (Remote)</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Note for remote URLs, in the <Code code='astro.config.js' lang="txt" inline /> you have to define the domains that are permitted to get remote images from.</p>

  <Code code='export default defineConfig({
  image: { domains: ["www.nps.gov"] },
});' lang="js" />

</Layout>
